  "_comment": "Game auto-detection fingerprints (watches the VOD's own OCR text, no user selection needed). Tokens must be DISTINCTIVE to one game -- menu/HUD/killfeed text unlikely to appear in another title, in chat, or in a stream overlay. Matching is whole-phrase, case-insensitive, after OCR normalization (uppercase, |/! -> I, 0 -> O, punctuation -> space) against every OCR string captured across the VOD (engines/reaction/game_detect.py). Detection needs >= 2 DISTINCT tokens, one unique winner, and >= 40% of all matched fingerprint evidence; repetition is never independent evidence. Every game therefore lists >= 3 plausible tokens. Rules (enforced by scripts/validate_signatures.py): no token under two games; no token also in scene_lexicon.json (menu text like BATTLE PASS shows in every game's lobby); no short/common single words. A false-positive fingerprint match misroutes the whole scan's hype lexicon + OCR event triggers -- when unsure, leave it out.",
